## Summary of this session (sess86)

**WIN — rename_visibility FIXED; cache_coherency went passed=1 → passed=2.**

**Diagnosis (RULE 4, instrumented):** The cache_coherency criterion runs each sub-test as a *separate* `run_tests.sh --test` invocation, with `rm -rf .mxfs_test` + recreate between them. So cross_visibility runs cold (passes), but rename/unlink/cwr each run on a warm cache after node1 recreated the dir tree — reusing inode numbers (confirmed: dir CT got inode 402900 before `rm` and 402900 again after `mkdir`; dir→dir, same number+type, only generation differs). node3/node4 got 20 `ENOTDIR` errors **at file-creation time** — their cached resolution of the recreated parent dir was a stale prior incarnation, so the files were never created and all their renames were "lost." It was never a dir-block lost-update. Every existing defense was blind because the reuse has **no type mismatch**, and d_revalidate only compared inode *numbers* (same after reuse → "valid") and ignored `XFS_ISTALE_CAW`.

**Fix (Gemini RULE-5 design A+C), build `5D6A63D2`, `pal/linux/xfs_super.c::mxfs_drevalidate`:**
- **A:** positive dentry with `i_dlm_stale || XFS_ISTALE_CAW` → return INVALID (before the own-AG fast-path) → xfs_lookup evicts + recycles fresh.
- **C:** peer-AG positive *directory* resolving to the same inode → lockless FUA read of on-disk `di_gen` (via existing `mxfs_inode_disk_di_size`, no ILOCK/DLM → no deadlock); if it differs from in-core `i_generation`, flag stale + return INVALID.

**Proven:** rename_visibility RUN2 went 81/240-fail → **PASS 240/240 (~11s)**; fix-path detectors all fired; no hang on a clean cluster.

**Remaining blocker:** unlink_visibility + cross_write_read. Decisively isolated this session — **unlink_visibility PASSES alone on a fresh mount (~25s, all 4 nodes)**, so my fix is innocent. The failure only appears in the full criterion sequence: a deep AG/defer corruption (`xfs_trans_cancel ← xfs_create`, `xfs_defer_finish_noroll`; the long-standing stochastic sess79–82 bnobt/defer family) shuts the FS down under the cumulative warm-cache + inode-reuse contamination, causing EIO → barrier timeouts → cwr can't run.

**Next session:** attack the create/defer corruption triggered by allocation into a reused-dir / stale-AG state under the contaminated multi-sub-test sequence (the create-path corruption is now the sole remaining cause of the cache_coherency FAIL). Progress and full context saved to `sess86_lessons.md`.

